# MQTT

Topic strings live only in `Constants.kt`. Do not hardcode `zerodata/...` elsewhere.

```kotlin
// BAD
mqtt.publish("zerodata/users/$id/inbox", payload)

// GOOD
mqtt.publish("${Constants.TOPIC_PREFIX}/$id/${Constants.TOPIC_INBOX_SUFFIX}", payload)
```

On-the-wire chat JSON is compact keys (`i`, `f`, `t`, `x`, `ts`) via `CompactMessageWire` / `MqttPayloadMapper`. Changing the wire requires both test phones on the same build.

Connection lifecycle stays in `MqttManager` implementations, driven through `ChatRepository`.
